  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q10-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "I have six identical balls in each of the colours blue, red and green. How many ways are there to choose six of these balls, without regard to order?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$28$",
      "worked": "A selection is determined by the numbers of blue, red and green balls. These are non-negative integers with total $6$; no colour needs more than the six balls available.\n\nRepresent the six selected balls by six stars and separate the three colour counts with two bars. Choose the positions of the bars among eight positions:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N &= \\binom{6+3-1}{3-1}\\\\N &= \\binom{8}{2}\\\\N &= 28.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
